From: OpenWrt WAVE maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] wave: bind cached station statistics to confirmed SID lifetimes

A new firmware station may reuse a SID while the MAC/PHY caches still contain
its predecessor. Assign a host incarnation only after STA_ADD confirmation,
retire it before SID release, and accept per-station cache data only from a
confirmed snapshot taken after that incarnation. A late iterator reference
cannot consume a replacement station's counters.

Use the existing PHY statistics mutex for MAC DMA publication and incarnation
changes too, so an older in-flight request cannot be tagged as the new station.
MAC-only measurements remain available without borrowing an old PHY duration.
Do not expose a PHY DMA buffer after an unsuccessful overwrite. None of these
changes assigns an ACK or retry-attempt meaning to firmware counters.

